uld shift a genuinely tied race toward Republicans in the final weeks.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Marcy Kaptur (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Marcy Kaptur, one of the House's longest-serving members, seeks another term in a northern Ohio district that leans Republican by about five points. She faces state Rep. Derek Merrin, a well-funded challenger, in what most analysts rate a genuine tossup with a slight Democratic edge. Kaptur holds a commanding cash advantage, roughly $3.5 million to Merrin's $0.5 million, and has used it to highlight federal investments in the Toledo area.\n\nThe polling picture is thin: a late-September DCCC poll showed the race tied at 48-48, while older Republican-sponsored surveys gave Merrin a modest lead. Prediction markets price Kaptur near 70%, and most expert ratings land at Lean D, though Inside Elections calls it Tilt R. Merrin has campaigned alongside gubernatorial candidate Vivek Ramaswamy, and trans-issue attacks have drawn attention from both directions. The race remains close, with Kaptur favored but clearly vulnerable.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7474, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7282, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7313, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7108, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6729, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6764, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7175, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7321, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7015, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7133, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7126, "margin": 3.0}]}